          },
          "pause": true,
          "displayType": "poster",
          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>The purine salvage pathway recycles free purine bases back into nucleotides. Whi</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>The purine salvage pathway recycles free purine bases back into nucleotides. Which enzyme is responsible for converting hypoxanthine to IMP and guanine to GMP in this pathway?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Xanthine oxidase</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Xanthine oxidase is a degradation enzyme — it converts purines to uric acid. The salvage pathway does the opposite: it recaptures bases for reuse.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Adenine phosphoribosyltransferase</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>APRT salvages adenine specifically, converting it to AMP. It does not handle hypoxanthine or guanine — those are HGPRT's substrates.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Hypoxanthine-guanine phosphoribosyltransferase</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. HGPRT recycles both hypoxanthine (→ IMP) and guanine (→ GMP). Its deficiency causes Lesch-Nyhan syndrome due to massively increased uric acid production.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>DNA polymerase III</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>DNA polymerase III synthesises new DNA strands during replication. It plays no role in nucleotide salvage or recycling of free bases.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "HGPRT (hypoxanthine-guanine phosphoribosyltransferase) handles salvage of both hypoxanthine and guanine. The brain and bone marrow depend heavily on this pathway because their capacity for energy-expensive de novo synthesis is limited."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "HGPRT is the key salvage enzyme, especially critical in the brain and bone marrow where de novo synthesis capacity is limited. Its complete deficiency causes Lesch-Nyhan syndrome."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
                "enableRetry": true,
